GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): the overworld drawn with an orthographic camera, its world
locked to the screen's pixels.

- GPU3D: with OrthoWanted (set by GoldLink while the game is in the overworld), a field
  perspective projection is replaced, once the camera matrix after it is known, by an
  orthographic one with the same angle and the same scale at the player's distance (the object
  nearest the screen's centre, learned once per camera setup and kept: no zoom), the
  camera shifted so the world's origin always lands at the same point within a pixel: the scene
  moves rigidly in whole pixels. Depth is the perspective's z/w matched in value and slope at
  that distance (the game's depth bias for sprites, shadows and the surf mount is kept), every w
  is a constant 64, the frame is Z-buffered. The shift goes with the frame through the swap and
  the render (OrthoShift, RenderOrthoShift, ShownOrthoShift) for GoldLink to slide the shown
  picture back by it at the screen's resolution. Rooms, which the game already draws
  orthographically, keep their projection and are only snapped.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

